## Brief Overview

---

Three Malaga Event Gear packages put you in charge of your own equipment, with no technician watching the levels: the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/), and the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) if you skip its technician add on. Each one has different gear, so what you check when something stops working is different too, not one generic checklist.

This guide walks through what our crew already tested before leaving, what to look at first on each of those three packages specifically, and who to call if a quick check does not fix it. [Contact us](/contact/) if you are unsure which package your booking falls under.

## Key Highlights

---

-   Three packages are genuinely self run: the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) and [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) have no technician option at all, and the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) only gets one if you pay for the add on.

-   We operate delivery only: our crew transports, installs, calibrates and tests every booking, including these three, before they ever leave your venue. The honest starting question is what changed since delivery, not what was broken from the start.

-   The self check that matters depends on what your package actually has. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) has no mixing console and no wireless microphone, so troubleshooting either one does not apply to it.

-   A wireless microphone only exists on the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/). The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/)'s gooseneck microphone is wired to the podium, so there is no battery or channel to check on it.

-   We are available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week for technical setups and live event monitoring, so a call is always an option once you have checked the obvious.

## Running Your Own Equipment: Which Packages Are Self Run

Not every package puts a technician on site, and the split is not close to even. Looking at our full catalog: the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) includes a technician for the whole event, and the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) includes one for up to 6 continuous hours. Neither of those is what this page is about. Our [technical support for events](/blog/technical-support-for-events/) guide covers what that technician actually does, phase by phase, if either of those describes your booking.

This page covers the other three packages instead:

-   **[Eco Pack](/packages/eco/).** No technician option at all, not even as a paid add on. Built as a self run PA system for a DJ or host controlling their own levels.
-   **[Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/).** No technician option at all either. Built for a corporate presentation, dealership showcase or product launch run by whoever is presenting.
-   **[Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/).** A technician is available, but only as a paid add on at 240 euros per day. If you did not add it, your booking is self run by default.

If none of that matches your package, our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide has the full technician by package breakdown.

