## Before You Troubleshoot: What Already Happened Before You Started

We do not offer a self collection or drop off option on any package. Every booking, including these three, arrives with our own crew, who deliver, install and test the equipment before they leave, confirming speakers are powered, the microphone is live, and a screen or projector is synced if your package includes one.

That matters for how you troubleshoot. If something is not working now, it worked when our crew left, so the honest first question is what has changed since then, not what might be broken. In practice that is almost always one of a small number of things: a cable that got knocked loose moving a table or a stand, a gain or volume control nudged by someone leaning on the console, a battery that has run down on a wireless handheld, or an input selected that does not match whichever laptop or device is actually connected right now.

For what that initial setup actually involves, gain staging and speaker placement adjusted to your specific venue rather than a fixed setting, see our [audio system calibration](/blog/audio-system-calibration/) guide. This page picks up from there: what to check if something changes after our crew leaves, not how it got calibrated to begin with.

## Self Check by Package: What to Look at First

What you check depends on what your package actually includes, since none of these three packages carry the same equipment.

| | [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) | [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) | [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) (no technician add on) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Speakers | 2 active speakers on stands | 2 speakers through a mixing console | Basic sound reinforcement system |
| Microphone | 1 wired dynamic microphone | 1 wireless handheld microphone | 1 wired gooseneck microphone (podium mounted) |
| Mixing console | None | Yes | None |
| Projector and screen | Not included (add on, +50 euros) | Yes, laser projector and screen | Yes, 3000 lumen projector and 2x2m screen |
| Lighting | 2 RGBW LED light bars | None | None |
| Technician | Not offered | Not offered | Optional add on, +240 euros per day |

### Eco Pack: No Console, No Wireless Mic

The Eco Pack is the simplest of the three, and that simplicity means fewer things to check. There is no mixing console and no wireless microphone in this package, so if a search result tells you to check a wireless receiver's channel, it does not apply here.

-   Check that both active speakers are still plugged into power and that the cable running from the mixing point to each speaker is fully seated.
-   Check the XLR cable on the wired dynamic microphone at both ends, at the mic itself and wherever it connects.
-   Check the power and connection on the RGBW LED light bars if the lighting looks off rather than the sound.
-   If you added the optional projector for +50 euros, its input source check works the same way as the Product Presentation Pack section below.

### Product Presentation Pack: Console, Projector and Wireless Mic

This is the package with the most to check, because it is the only one of the three with both a mixing console and a wireless microphone.

-   Check the mixing console for a channel that has been muted or a gain fader nudged down, most commonly from someone leaning on the desk or a bag set down on it.
-   Check that the input channel selected on the console matches the laptop or device actually connected right now, especially if more than one person has plugged in during the event.
-   Check the wireless handheld microphone's battery level and confirm it is set to the same channel as its receiver. A dropped connection is most often one of those two things, not a fault with the unit itself.
-   Check the projector's input source selection (HDMI or the port in use) against the connected laptop, and confirm the screen is showing the same resolution the projector expects.
-   Check that every cable, HDMI, XLR and speaker, is still seated at both ends. This is the single most common cause across all three packages.

### Basic MICE Pack Without the Technician Add On

Without the add on, the Basic MICE Pack has no mixing console to check and no wireless microphone either, its gooseneck microphone is wired directly to the podium.

-   Check the projector's input source against whichever laptop is connected, the same check as the Product Presentation Pack above.
-   Check the gooseneck microphone's cable connection at the base of the podium.
-   Check that the sound reinforcement system's power and speaker cables are still seated, since there is no console fader to isolate the problem to instead.

## Feedback or Buzzing From the Speakers

This one is not specific to any single package. Feedback, the rising squeal when a microphone picks up its own amplified sound, usually means the microphone has moved closer to a speaker or is now pointed toward one, so moving it or turning slightly away is the first thing to try. A steady buzz or hum more often points to a cable run crossing a power cable, or a loose connection at either end, so retracing the cable path and reseating both ends is worth doing before assuming anything is faulty.

## Who to Call When It Goes Beyond a Quick Fix

Check the obvious first: cables, gain, battery, input selection. If that does not resolve it, we are available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week for technical setups and live event monitoring, on every booking, including these three self run packages. [Contact us](/contact/) or call 600 42 87 50 if you need us mid event.

## Want a Technician Instead of Troubleshooting It Yourself

If reading this makes you wish someone else was handling it, that is a real option on two of these three packages. Our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide covers which package to add one to and what it costs, and our [technical support for events](/blog/technical-support-for-events/) guide covers what that technician actually does once they are on site. The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) can add one for 240 euros per day. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) and [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) do not offer one at any price, so if a technician is a hard requirement for your event, the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) or [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) are the packages that include one as standard instead. And if you have not booked yet at all, our [AV equipment consultations](/blog/av-equipment-consultations/) guide covers matching your event to the right package before you get to this page.

## Is Troubleshooting Different Outdoors

The checks themselves are the same, cables, gain, battery, input selection, but an outdoor booking adds cable exposure and wind to the list of things that can knock a connection loose in the first place. See our [audio visual rental for outdoor events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-outdoor-events/) guide for how we plan cable runs and stand placement outdoors before your event even starts.

